From d8f5dad43a8543b2fbb918ec1ac6d18c64976b28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:55:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 217/219] fix: gate the blend layer at a ray hit so ConeTracePS
 fits fxc again

Stopgap for the capacity wall measured in report 06a section 6 (option 2); the
real fix is moving the material reconstruction into ShadePS, which follows as its
own task.

ConeTracePS holds the voxel cone tracer, the BVH walk and RT_ProcessBestHit in one
entry point, and fxc cannot build it: "internal error: compilation aborted
unexpectedly" on the engine's real specular flag set, with both the Windows SDK
compiler (10.0.26100.7705) and the one Sandbox.exe loads from System32
(10.0.26100.9444), at every optimisation level and on ps_4_0 / ps_5_0 / ps_5_1.
The minimisation in 06a showed the overdraft is smaller than either half of
RT_ProcessBestHit's %BLENDLAYER block, while removing two of the three
RT_TraverseTris instantiations does not help at all - the limit counts RT code
reachable from ConeTracePS, not shader size.

So the %BLENDLAYER reconstruction is gated behind a plain
`#define RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER 0`, not a %-flag: there is no permutation in which it
is generated today and the switch is one line to flip back. The code is kept
verbatim. `RT_HIT_DETAIL_MAP` is the documented second cut and stays 1 - gating
the blend layer alone bought the headroom, and detail mapping shows on every
material rather than on the few authored with a second layer.

GAP: blend layer at a ray hit is deferred to the ShadePS material-reconstruction
move. A %BLENDLAYER material - a wall whose second layer is painted-on dirt or
moss - reflects with its base layer only: base albedo, normal, smoothness and
reflectance. The mask, the blend record and the falloff are still produced on the
CPU and still sit in the extras record; nothing but the gated block reads them.

Harness (exit-code based failure test): 33/33 green with BOTH compilers,
cryfx_lint.py clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 .../Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi  | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
index b75bec87..e297875d 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
@@ -85,6 +85,31 @@ float4 SVO_RTParams1;
 // Traversal stack depth: e_svoTI_RT_MaxDepth (18) + 2.
 #define VOX_RT_MAX_CALL_STACK              20
 
+///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+// Hit material reconstruction budget (2026-09-14, report 06a section 6, option 2).
+//
+// ConeTracePS holds the voxel cone tracer, the BVH walk and RT_ProcessBestHit in one entry
+// point, and that is over fxc's capacity: it answers "internal error: compilation aborted
+// unexpectedly" on the engine's real specular permutation, with both the Windows SDK compiler
+// and the one the engine loads, at every optimisation level. Measured headroom on the commit
+// before this one: the shader compiles as soon as EITHER HALF of the %BLENDLAYER block below
+// is removed, and it still fails if a whole RT_TraverseTris instantiation (two of the three)
+// is removed instead - the limit counts RT code reachable from ConeTracePS, not shader size.
+//
+// So the blend layer is gated OFF here as a stopgap. These are plain macros, not %-flags:
+// there is no permutation in which the code is generated today, and the switch is a single
+// line to flip once the real fix lands.
+//
+// GAP: blend layer at a ray hit is deferred to the ShadePS material-reconstruction move
+// (report 06a section 6 option 1). A %BLENDLAYER material - a wall whose second layer is a
+// painted-on dirt or moss - reflects with its BASE layer only: base albedo, base normal, base
+// smoothness, base reflectance. The mask, the blend record and the falloff are all still
+// produced on the CPU and still sit in the extras record; nothing but this block reads them.
+// Detail mapping is deliberately left ON - it is the one of the two that shows on every
+// material rather than on the few that are authored with a second layer.
+#define RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER                 0
+#define RT_HIT_DETAIL_MAP                  1
+
 #define VOX_RT_MAX_BOUNCES                 (SVO_RTParams0.x)
 #define VOX_RT_GLOSS_SCALE                 (SVO_RTParams0.y)
 #define VOX_RT_MIX_WITH_PROBES             (SVO_RTParams0.z)
@@ -1113,7 +1138,11 @@ void RT_ProcessBestHit(const Ray rOrig, inout SRTInfo rtInfo, const float fDista
 		// GetLayerBlendingValue's vtxAlpha is substituted with 1: the triangle record has no
 		// vertex colour lane (report 05A section 3), so a vertex painted blend shows at its
 		// authored strength everywhere instead of only where it was painted.
+		//
+		// GATED OFF by RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER - see the macro at the top of this file. The code is
+		// kept verbatim so that flipping the macro back to 1 is the whole change.
 		///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+#if RT_HIT_BLEND_LAYER
 		if (bExtras && vEx1.x > 0.f)
 		{
 			const int nSlotMask = (int)vEx1.y - 1;
@@ -1155,6 +1184,7 @@ void RT_ProcessBestHit(const Ray rOrig, inout SRTInfo rtInfo, const float fDista
 				                       fBlendFac);
 			}
 		}
+#endif
 
 		///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 		// %DETAIL_MAPPING (Illum.cfx:548-559, identical in Vegetation.cfx:482 and
@@ -1174,7 +1204,13 @@ void RT_ProcessBestHit(const Ray rOrig, inout SRTInfo rtInfo, const float fDista
 		// The bump half is multiplied by the same distance fade the base normal map gets, so a
 		// far away detail-mapped wall flattens as one surface instead of losing only half of
 		// its relief.
+		//
+		// Kept ON: RT_HIT_DETAIL_MAP is the second budget switch (see the macro at the top of
+		// this file) and gating the blend layer alone bought the headroom, so this one has
+		// never been off. It is here so the next person who runs out of room knows where the
+		// second cut is, and does not have to find it again.
 		///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+#if RT_HIT_DETAIL_MAP
 		if (bExtras)
 		{
 			const int nSlotDetail = (int)ExtractUint2(vEx0.x).x - 1;
@@ -1190,6 +1226,7 @@ void RT_ProcessBestHit(const Ray rOrig, inout SRTInfo rtInfo, const float fDista
 				vHitAlbedo     += vHitAlbedo * (vDetail.z * vDetailScales.x);
 			}
 		}
+#endif
 
 		///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 		// Per type parameters (decision 10, report 05A section 2.1). One float3 plus one 8 bit
-- 
